Subject: [PATCH] of: reserved_mem: refresh dynamic region names after FDT copy

Dynamic regions are recorded before MIPS copies its appended DTB out of
init memory. Their names still point into the old blob when the reserved
memory table is used by modules after free_initmem(). Static regions are
already recorded from the copied blob in fdt_scan_reserved_mem_reg_nodes().

Refresh existing dynamic-region names from the current blob before scanning
the static regions. Node offsets remain valid across the byte-for-byte copy.
Keep the original allocation geometry and reservation lifetime unchanged.

--- a/drivers/of/of_reserved_mem.c
+++ b/drivers/of/of_reserved_mem.c
@@ -191,6 +191,14 @@ void __init fdt_scan_reserved_mem_reg_nodes(void)
 	if (!fdt)
 		return;
 
+	/* The FDT may have been copied since dynamic regions were saved.
+	 * Do not retain names in the original, potentially init-only blob.
+	 */
+	for (int i = 0; i < reserved_mem_count; i++) {
+		struct reserved_mem *rmem = &reserved_mem[i];
+
+		rmem->name = fdt_get_name(fdt, rmem->fdt_node, NULL);
+	}
 	node = fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/reserved-memory");
 	if (node < 0) {
 		pr_info("Reserved memory: No reserved-memory node in the DT\n");
